PROPOSAL ONLY -- DO NOT APPLY WITHOUT THE USER'S APPROVAL.
==========================================================

`realm/sim_config.py` lives on the main port branch and the user has not approved a change to it.
This file exists so the proposal is reviewable as a diff rather than as prose. Nothing applies it.

WHAT IT ADDS
    A fourth `rendering_mode`, "r111", that reproduces OmniGibson 1.1.1's renderer configuration on
    the 3.9.1 stack. Two parts, and the second is the half that is easy to forget:

      1. the eight carb values 1.1.1's `_set_renderer_settings` produces under
         `gm.ENABLE_HQ_RENDERING = True` (OG-lite/omnigibson/simulator.py:480-496), and
      2. turning OFF the five things OG 3.9.1 sets that 1.1.1 never touches --
         `rendermode = RealTimePathTracing`, `rtx/modes/rt/enabled`, `rtx/modes/rt2/enabled`,
         `raytracing/fractionalCutoutOpacity`, `flow/enabled`.

WHY IT DOES NOT TOUCH gm.ENABLE_HQ_RENDERING
    Because it must not. Setting that macro True on 3.9.1 trips
    `assert (1 / self.get_rendering_dt()) >= 60` (simulator.py:700) at REALM's 15 Hz, and the
    cascade behind it is three asserts deep -- raising the render rate then trips
    `sim_step_dt == rendering_dt` under `gm.HEADLESS`, and raising the sim rate then trips
    robot.py:488 against `control_freq: 15`, hardcoded twice in every realm/config/robots/*.yaml.
    Applying the carb values the HQ branch WOULD have produced sidesteps all three, and the macro's
    only other effect in 3.9.1 outside an isosurface-only block is `dlss/execMode`, which is set
    explicitly here anyway.

WHY IT IS NOT THE EXISTING "r" BRANCH
    "r" is not a revert to 1.1.1, it is a third look. It sets `RaytracedLighting` but ALSO disables
    shadows, reflections, indirectDiffuse and ambientOcclusion, and leaves ambient at 1.0 -- and it
    measures BRIGHTER than the 3.9.1 default, not darker (exterior cam1 206.20 vs 173.34, against
    1.1.1's 117.99). Do not reach for "r" expecting 1.1.1's look.

TIMING -- LOAD-BEARING
    `set_rendering_mode()` is called from `env_dynamic.finalize_setup()`, i.e. after env creation but
    BEFORE the scene has ever been rendered. That is the right place and it is why this belongs here
    rather than in a post-hoc helper: the same settings applied after warmup are worth measurably
    less (`rendering_mode="r"` scores +9.8% on exterior cam1 applied post-warmup vs +20.0% applied
    here). Any caller that wants this must go through `rendering_mode`, not set carb keys later.

BEFORE PROPOSING THIS AS A FIX, READ THE MEASUREMENT
    `r111` was measured on og391 and it does NOT restore 1.1.1's appearance -- see
    ~/runbook/streams/realm_og391_port.md. It is worth adding as a *documented, faithful* control so
    nobody has to re-derive what 1.1.1 actually configured, not as a repair. The residual gap is not
    a carb setting.

